        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "An employee holding a position in the competitive class on a permanent basis for at least one (1) year who is appointed to serve in a position in the County service which is in the exempt class or non-competitive class or in the unclassified service may at the discretion of the appointing authority, be granted a leave of absence without pay during such service for a period not exceeding one (1) year. Such leave of absence may, at the discretion of the appointing authority and with the approval of the Niagara County Personnel Officer, be renewed, provided, however, that no such leave of absence without pay shall extend beyond four (4) years from the date such employee left the competitive class position. Any employee who leaves the County service without an approved leave of absence loses all service and seniority rights.",
